    "section": "scientific-foundations",
    "domain": "Nutrition",
    "topic": "Supplement Safety",
    "cognitiveLevel": "Analysis",
    "text": "A recreational client already consumes about 400 mg of caffeine daily from coffee and now wants to add a pre-workout supplement containing 300 mg of caffeine plus 20 mg of synephrine per serving before an afternoon training session. Which safety concern is most directly supported by the evidence?",
